---
functor: 1
title: ceil
---

set heading(numbering: none)

`ceil` · fence · round up.

# Form

`(a + b).ceil` on a group, `x.ceil` on a symbol.

# Examples

| Recipe | Result | Glyph |
|:--|:-:|:--|
| `(x).ceil` | $(x).ceil$ | fence around the group |

# Four layers

| Layer | For this operation |
|:--|:--|
| Meaning | Round up. A guideline, not a rule. |
| Style | A kind can take this fence from a rule: `set abs(fence: ceil)`. |
| Construction | Brackets around a group or a symbol. The brackets grow with the content. |
| Glyph | The font glyph when the font has one, otherwise a built glyph kept in the recipe cache. |

# Rules

- Works on a group, `(a + b).ceil`, or on a symbol, `x.ceil`. Write `x2` after it to double the fence. Write `left` or `right` after it to keep one side only. A style rule can give a kind its fence: `set mat(fence: ceil)`.

# From LaTeX

`\lceil x \rceil` becomes `(x).ceil` or `ceil(x)`.

